Feature: Interactive Placement — Click-to-Select & Draw-to-Place with SAM3 + pikaswaps
  As an editor placing brand assets into video
  I want to click on objects in the video or draw a region on blank surfaces
  So that SAM3 video-rle segments/tracks my selection with per-frame RLE masks, pikaswaps swaps in the asset via text prompts, and planar warp places signage pixel-perfect

  Background:
    Given the BIT platform has ingested video content
    And brand assets are uploaded to a campaign
    And SAM3 video-rle (fal-ai/sam-3/video-rle) and pikaswaps API keys are configured in Platform Settings
    And SAM3 video-rle returns per-frame SAM3VideoObjectFrame with SAM3ObjectMask (RLE + track_id)

  # ── Click-to-Segment (Generative Path — 3D Products via pikaswaps) ──

  Scenario: Click on an existing billboard segments it via SAM3 video-rle
    Given I am in the Placement Editor with "Insert Product" mode active
    When I click on a billboard in the video player
    Then a call is made to SAM3 video-rle with the clicked (x, y) point_prompt at that frame
    And SAM3 returns a SAM3VideoObjectFrame with the RLE mask for the clicked object
    And the RLE mask is decoded to a polygon via RleDecoder
    And the polygon is rendered as a colored SVG overlay on the video
    And the AssetType is set to "Generative"

  Scenario: Click on background returns no usable mask
    Given I click on an empty sky region with no distinct object
    When SAM3 video-rle processes the point prompt
    Then no object with confidence > 0.5 is returned
    And the UI shows "No distinct surface found — try 'Place Signage' mode instead"

  Scenario: SAM3 video-rle returns stable track_id for the clicked object
    Given SAM3 video-rle returns a mask for the clicked object
    When the response includes SAM3ObjectMask with a track_id
    Then the track_id is stable across all frames where that object appears
    And the track_id is stored on the SurfaceItem for drift-check comparison
    And the mask polygon is stored in BoundaryCoordinatesJson

  Scenario: Mask overlay updates when user changes frame
    Given a mask overlay is visible for the current frame
    When the user scrubs to a different frame
    Then the overlay is hidden (preview mask is frame-specific)
    And a "Re-detect at this frame" button appears

  # ── Draw-to-Place (Planar Path — Signage / Flat Assets) ──

  Scenario: Place a logo on a wall via 4-corner quad
    Given I am in the Placement Editor with "Place Signage" mode active
    When I click 4 corners of the wall region where the logo should go
    Then a quadrilateral overlay is displayed with draggable corner handles
    And numbered corner badges (1-4) are shown during placement
    And the UI shows a live perspective preview of the logo warped into that quad
    And the AssetType is set to "Planar"

  Scenario: Fine-tune quad by dragging corners
    Given a 4-corner quad overlay is visible
    When I drag any corner handle
    Then the quad updates to reflect the new corner position
    And the perspective preview refreshes in real time
    And the polygon coordinates update in real time

  Scenario: SAM3 video-rle refines quad to match wall perspective
    Given a 4-corner quad overlay is confirmed
    When the user clicks "Refine with AI"
    Then SAM3 video-rle receives the quad as box_prompts
    And SAM3 returns a refined polygon that follows wall edges and texture
    And the overlay updates to show the refined quad

  Scenario: Cancel quad placement
    Given a quad overlay is visible
    When the user clicks "Cancel" or presses Escape
    Then the overlay is removed
    And no data is persisted

  # ── Approval & Render Dispatch ──

  Scenario: Approve generative placement triggers pikaswaps render
    Given a mask overlay is displayed and the user has selected an asset
    When the user clicks "Approve & Render"
    Then a SurfaceItem is created with AssetType="Generative" and Source="Manual"
    And the SAM3 mask polygon and track_id are stored on the SurfaceItem
    And Gemini generates modify_region (describes region to replace) and prompt (describes desired result) from the surface type and asset
    And a Hangfire job is enqueued for pikaswaps compositing (video + image + modify_region + prompt)
    And the UI shows render progress via SignalR

  Scenario: Approve planar placement triggers homography render
    Given a quad overlay is displayed and the user has selected a flat asset
    When the user clicks "Approve & Render"
    Then a SurfaceItem is created with AssetType="Planar" and Source="Manual"
    And a Hangfire job is enqueued for point tracking → planar warp compositing
    And the UI shows render progress via SignalR

  # ── Generative Path: pikaswaps Compositing (text-driven, no mask input) ──

  Scenario: pikaswaps swaps asset using text description of region
    Given a generative render job is processing
    When the Hangfire job reaches compositing
    Then pikaswaps is called with: video_url, image_url (brand asset), modify_region (text describing object to replace), and prompt (text describing desired result)
    And pikaswaps uses its own internal AI to locate the region from the modify_region text
    And no SAM3 mask video is sent to pikaswaps — the API has no mask_url or mask parameter
    And SAM3 data is only used for: (1) UI preview overlay, (2) drift-check comparison after render

  Scenario: Gemini generates modify_region and prompt for pikaswaps
    Given a surface has SurfaceType "Stadium Perimeter LED Board" and a brand asset is selected
    When the render job prepares the pikaswaps payload
    Then Gemini generates modify_region describing the object to replace (e.g. "the LED perimeter board on the field")
    And Gemini generates prompt describing how the asset should look (e.g. "replace with a Coca-Cola advertisement, photorealistic, matching stadium lighting")
    And both strings are included in the pikaswaps API call

  Scenario: pikaswaps 5-second limit requires chunking
    Given a generative placement scene is 12 seconds long
    When the render job reaches compositing
    Then the source video is split into 3 chunks of ≤5 seconds with 0.25s overlap
    And each chunk is processed through pikaswaps independently with the same image_url, modify_region, and prompt
    And the chunks are spliced back into a single video via ffmpeg concat

  Scenario: Chunk failure is retried independently
    Given chunk 2 of 3 failed during pikaswaps processing
    When the render job retries
    Then only chunk 2 is re-processed
    And chunks 1 and 3 are not re-processed

  Scenario: All chunks fail falls back to ffmpeg luma-mask
    Given all pikaswaps chunks failed after retries
    Then SAM3 video is generated from the stored mask polygon (lazy fallback tracking via sam-3/video endpoint)
    And ffmpeg luma-mask compositing is used
    And the RenderItem shows CompositingEngine="ffmpeg-luma" and QualityTier="Standard"
    Given all pikaswaps chunks failed
    When retries are exhausted
    Then the render falls back to ffmpeg luma-mask compositing
    And the RenderItem shows CompositingEngine="ffmpeg-luma" and QualityTier="Standard"

  # ── Generative Path: Post-Render Drift Check (uses SAM3 video-rle RLE data) ──

  Scenario: pikaswaps output passes drift consistency check
    Given a pikaswaps render has completed
    When the post-render drift check runs SAM3 video-rle on the output video
    And per-frame RLE masks for the same track_id are compared to the original preview mask
    And per-frame mask IoU is ≥ 0.85 for all frames
    Then the render is marked "Finished" with QualityTier "AI"

  Scenario: pikaswaps output fails drift check
    Given a pikaswaps render has completed
    When the post-render drift check runs SAM3 video-rle on the output
    And any frame has mask IoU < 0.85 against the original track_id mask
    Then the render is marked "NeedsReview"
    And an ⚠️ badge is shown in the Renders list
    And the Admin can approve or regenerate the render

  # ── Planar Path: Point Tracking & Warp ──

  Scenario: Quad corners are tracked across frames
    Given a planar placement has been approved
    When the render job begins
    Then the 4 corner points are tracked across all scene frames via point tracking
    And per-frame quad coordinates are stored (not masks)
    And tracking lock-loss on any corner is flagged

  Scenario: Signage asset is perspective-warped per frame
    Given per-frame quad coordinates are available for all frames
    When the planar compositing engine processes the render
    Then the signage PNG is perspective-warped to match each frame's quad
    And the warped image preserves exact pixel content (no AI regeneration)
    And the output matches the original logo pixel-for-pixel

  Scenario: Signage lighting matches wall via classical relighting
    Given a warped signage frame
    When the relighting pass runs
    Then a luminance histogram transfer is applied from the surrounding wall region
    And the signage appears naturally lit without modifying logo content

  Scenario: Person occludes signage — SAM3 video-rle provides foreground mask
    Given a person crosses in front of the wall signage during the scene
    When the compositing engine processes those frames
    Then SAM3 video-rle is called to return per-frame RLE masks for any foreground objects
    And the warped signage is subtracted where foreground masks overlap

  Scenario: Quad tracking loses lock
    Given the surface corner moves out of frame or is fully occluded
    When point tracking loses lock on one or more corners
    Then the render is marked "Failed" with error "Quad tracking lost lock at frame N"
    And the specific corner and frame are logged

  Scenario: Planar path has no duration limit
    Given a 60-second scene with a wall signage placement
    When the planar compositing engine processes the render
    Then the full 60 seconds are processed in a single pass
    And no chunking or splicing is needed

  # ── Engine Tagging & Quality Visibility ──

  Scenario: Render record tracks which compositing engine was used
    Given a render has completed
    When I view the render details
    Then the CompositingEngine field shows the actual engine used
    And the QualityTier field shows "AI", "Exact", or "Standard"

  Scenario: UI surfaces quality tier to user
    Given the Renders list shows completed renders
    Then pikaswaps renders show 🟣 "AI Enhanced" badge
    And planar warp renders show 🟢 "Pixel Perfect" badge
    And ffmpeg fallback renders show ⚪ "Standard" badge
    And hovering ⚪ shows tooltip explaining AI enhancement was unavailable

  # ── Mode Switching ──

  Scenario: Toggle between Insert Product and Place Signage modes
    Given I am in the Placement Editor
    When I toggle the interaction mode
    Then "Insert Product" mode shows a crosshair cursor for object selection
    And "Place Signage" mode shows corner-placement cursor with "Click 4 corners" instruction
    And switching modes clears any active overlay
